patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/admin/services/data/settings
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{authToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "isEnabled": true,
    "activeProvider": "ujaydata",
    "userMarkupPercent": 15,
    "vendorMarkupPercent": 10,
    "roundingMode": "ceil",
    "userPricingTiers": [
      { "minCost": 0, "maxCost": 500, "markupPercent": 15 },
      { "minCost": 501, "maxCost": 1500, "markupPercent": 10 },
      { "minCost": 1501, "maxCost": 3000, "markupPercent": 7 },
      { "minCost": 3001, "maxCost": 6000, "markupPercent": 5 },
      { "minCost": 6001, "maxCost": null, "markupPercent": 3 }
    ],
    "vendorPricingTiers": [
      { "minCost": 0, "maxCost": 500, "markupPercent": 10 },
      { "minCost": 501, "maxCost": 1500, "markupPercent": 7 },
      { "minCost": 1501, "maxCost": 3000, "markupPercent": 5 },
      { "minCost": 3001, "maxCost": 6000, "markupPercent": 3 },
      { "minCost": 6001, "maxCost": null, "markupPercent": 2 }
    ]
  }
}

docs {
  # Admin Update Data Settings

  Admin updates data service provider and markup settings.

  Use this request when admin wants to:

  - switch between `smeapi` and `ujaydata`
  - change normal user profit margin
  - change vendor profit margin
  - make big data plans cheaper using tiered pricing

  This request must be sent as raw JSON with:

  ```txt
  Content-Type: application/json
  ```

  If the body is not sent as JSON, the backend will not receive the fields correctly.

  ## Endpoint

  `PATCH /api/v1/admin/services/data/settings`

  ## Authentication

  Admin JWT required.

  ## Body Fields

  `isEnabled`
  Use `true` to allow data purchases or `false` to temporarily disable data service.

  `activeProvider`
  Supported values are `smeapi` and `ujaydata`.

  `smeapi` is the primary data provider. `ujaydata` is the backup provider. Admin can switch this value anytime and the frontend endpoints will stay the same.

  `userMarkupPercent`
  Fallback percentage added on top of provider cost price for normal users.

  If `userPricingTiers` is set and a plan cost falls inside a tier, the tier markup is used instead.

  `vendorMarkupPercent`
  Fallback percentage added on top of provider cost price for active vendors.

  If `vendorPricingTiers` is set and a plan cost falls inside a tier, the tier markup is used instead.

  `userPricingTiers`
  Optional. Tiered pricing for normal users. Use this to make small plans profitable and big plans cheaper.

  Each tier has:

  - `minCost`: provider cost price starts from this amount
  - `maxCost`: provider cost price ends at this amount, or `null` for no upper limit
  - `markupPercent`: percentage to add for plans inside this cost range

  `vendorPricingTiers`
  Optional. Tiered pricing for active vendors.

  Send an empty array `[]` if you want to remove tiered pricing and go back to flat percentage.

  `roundingMode`
  Use `ceil` to round up to the next naira, or `round` to round normally.

  ## Recommended MVP Tier Structure

  This structure keeps small plans profitable but prevents large plans from becoming too expensive:

  ```txt
  Normal users:
  Cost 0 - 500       => 15%
  Cost 501 - 1500    => 10%
  Cost 1501 - 3000   => 7%
  Cost 3001 - 6000   => 5%
  Cost 6001 and above => 3%

  Vendors:
  Cost 0 - 500       => 10%
  Cost 501 - 1500    => 7%
  Cost 1501 - 3000   => 5%
  Cost 3001 - 6000   => 3%
  Cost 6001 and above => 2%
  ```

  ## How Tier Matching Works

  Backend checks the provider `costPrice` and finds the first tier where:

  ```txt
  costPrice >= minCost
  and
  costPrice <= maxCost
  ```

  If `maxCost` is `null`, it means there is no upper limit.

  Example:

  ```txt
  MTN 36GB costPrice = 10700
  It matches { "minCost": 6001, "maxCost": null, "markupPercent": 3 }
  User selling price = 10700 + 3% = 11021
  Profit = 321
  ```

  Without tiered pricing, 15% would make that plan:

  ```txt
  10700 + 15% = 12305
  Profit = 1605
  ```

  That is too expensive for big packages, so tiered pricing is better.

  ## Example

  To switch to UjayData with tiered pricing:

  ```json
  {
    "isEnabled": true,
    "activeProvider": "ujaydata",
    "userMarkupPercent": 15,
    "vendorMarkupPercent": 10,
    "roundingMode": "ceil",
    "userPricingTiers": [
      { "minCost": 0, "maxCost": 500, "markupPercent": 15 },
      { "minCost": 501, "maxCost": 1500, "markupPercent": 10 },
      { "minCost": 1501, "maxCost": 3000, "markupPercent": 7 },
      { "minCost": 3001, "maxCost": 6000, "markupPercent": 5 },
      { "minCost": 6001, "maxCost": null, "markupPercent": 3 }
    ],
    "vendorPricingTiers": [
      { "minCost": 0, "maxCost": 500, "markupPercent": 10 },
      { "minCost": 501, "maxCost": 1500, "markupPercent": 7 },
      { "minCost": 1501, "maxCost": 3000, "markupPercent": 5 },
      { "minCost": 3001, "maxCost": 6000, "markupPercent": 3 },
      { "minCost": 6001, "maxCost": null, "markupPercent": 2 }
    ]
  }
  ```

  To switch back to flat markup only, send empty arrays:

  ```json
  {
    "isEnabled": true,
    "activeProvider": "smeapi",
    "userMarkupPercent": 15,
    "vendorMarkupPercent": 10,
    "roundingMode": "ceil",
    "userPricingTiers": [],
    "vendorPricingTiers": []
  }
  ```

  ## Price Calculation

  If provider price is `N199` and the matched user markup is `15`, frontend will see:

  ```txt
  N199 + 15% = N228.85
  ceil = N229
  ```

  If provider price is `N10,700` and the matched user markup is `3`, frontend will see:

  ```txt
  N10,700 + 3% = N11,021
  profit = N321
  ```

  ## Frontend/Admin Dashboard Notes

  The admin dashboard should allow admin to edit:

  - active provider
  - fallback normal user markup
  - fallback vendor markup
  - user pricing tiers
  - vendor pricing tiers
  - rounding mode

  The user app does not call this endpoint. Only admin dashboard should call it.

  The user app should only fetch final plan prices from:

  ```txt
  GET /api/v1/services/data/plans
  ```

  Do not calculate markup on the frontend. Backend already returns final `sellingPrice`.

  ## Expected Response

  ```json
  {
    "message": "Data service settings updated successfully",
    "settings": {
      "service": "data",
      "isEnabled": true,
      "activeProvider": "ujaydata",
      "userMarkupPercent": 15,
      "vendorMarkupPercent": 10,
      "roundingMode": "ceil",
      "userPricingTiers": [
        {
          "minCost": 0,
          "maxCost": 500,
          "markupPercent": 15
        }
      ],
      "vendorPricingTiers": [
        {
          "minCost": 0,
          "maxCost": 500,
          "markupPercent": 10
        }
      ]
    }
  }
  ```
}
